 the same way.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected` in `tests/tests.rs`. It runs `fd foo --and one/two` and expects the error. It failed before the fix and passes after.\n\n**Verified:**\n- `cargo test -q` passes: 139 unit tests and 111 integration tests.\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` finds nothing in `src/`. It does report about 14 `useless_borrows_in_formatting` errors in `tests/tests.rs`, but they were there before my change; I didn't touch them.\n\n**Not run:**\n- `cargo fmt`, because rustfmt isn't installed. I kept the edited line under 100 characters by hand.\n- The Windows-only branch wasn't compiled on this machine.\n\nTo commit, set `user.name` and `user.email` and run `git commit -a`. The message I'd use is \"Flag path separators in --and patterns too\".","ttft_ms":3086,"type":"result","duration_ms":110933,"uuid":"4e8ff1a7-2c32-4708-96a4-9497d73ef4cc","ttft_stream_ms":2162,"time_to_request_ms":91,"first_content_frame_ms":2162,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
